00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:48.129
So while my Russian buddy,
Eric, can't join me,

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:49.721
I've luckily met Kristina here

00:00:49.721 --> 00:00:52.970
to help me out as I explore
the Russian capital.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.368
How do you say cow in Russian?

00:00:54.368 --> 00:00:55.394
- [Kristina] (speaks in foreign language)

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:58.885
- (speaks foreign language)

00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:00.468
What does that say?

00:01:00.768 --> 00:01:02.346
- [Kristina] McDonald's.

00:01:02.346 --> 00:01:03.179
Cool.

00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:05.936
- [Kristina] You can now break the law.

00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:09.526
- This is an international
terrorist incident.

00:01:09.526 --> 00:01:12.501
- [Kristina] (speaks foreign language)

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.380
- (speaks foreign language)

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.393
- [Kristina] (speaks foreign language)

00:01:17.393 --> 00:01:19.310
We're here in a square.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.651
Alright, so we're at this Georgian place.

00:01:21.651 --> 00:01:22.732
What's the name of the restaurant?

00:01:22.732 --> 00:01:23.565
- (speaks foreign language)

00:01:23.565 --> 00:01:26.688
- (speaks foreign language)
- (laughs) You won't manage.

00:01:26.688 --> 00:01:28.074
- What are things, I guess you think,

00:01:28.074 --> 00:01:29.989
I should know or be aware of about Russia?

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.069
- Russia's a big country, really very big,

00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:34.236
and it has a lot of people

00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:36.397
and people are really very different.

00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:38.730
Some people are open minded.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.861
They want to be friends
with all over the world,

00:01:41.861 --> 00:01:43.847
and some people hate everyone.

00:01:43.847 --> 00:01:47.180
I think it's because their life is hard,

00:01:47.351 --> 00:01:50.243
because life in Russia
sometimes is very, very hard.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.660
We have a lot of poor people.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:56.369
We have lots of problems
inside the country,

00:01:56.369 --> 00:02:00.202
but we have to make our
life better ourselves.

00:02:00.621 --> 00:02:02.082
No one will help us.

00:02:02.082 --> 00:02:03.973
Not the government, not the President,

00:02:03.973 --> 00:02:06.723
only we can make our life better.

00:02:07.064 --> 00:02:09.082
- To learn more about daily life here,

00:02:09.082 --> 00:02:11.889
I decided to chat with some locals.

00:02:11.889 --> 00:02:12.722
(speaks in foreign language)

00:02:12.722 --> 00:02:13.555
- Hello.

00:02:13.555 --> 00:02:14.470
- You know, we should trade music,

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.309
so you know, what's a good Russian artist?

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:19.054
- (speaks in foreign language)

00:02:19.054 --> 00:02:22.804
- (speaks foreign language)

00:02:22.837 --> 00:02:23.797
- [Kristina] Do you like it already?

00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:25.233
- I'm digging it, Kristina.

00:02:25.233 --> 00:02:26.066
(Kristina laughs)

00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:31.066
♪ (singing in foreign language) ♪

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:36.572
Do you guys watch or listen
to Western music, media, TV?

00:02:36.572 --> 00:02:37.520
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.810
- [Kristina] The Big Bang Theory.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.030
- Big Bang Theory? (laughs)

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.702
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:02:41.702 --> 00:02:43.285
- Rihanna, Beyonce.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:44.340
- I'm not a big Beyonce fan.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.018
- (speaks foreign language)
- Are you not? How come?

00:02:46.018 --> 00:02:47.678
- Wow, that's a face even Americans make

00:02:47.678 --> 00:02:49.838
when I tell people that.
(women laughing)

00:02:49.838 --> 00:02:51.151
No, I'm more of a Michael Bublé guy.

00:02:51.151 --> 00:02:52.609
Do you guys like Michael Bublé?

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:53.609
- Who is it?

00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:57.436
- Michael Bublé?

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:00.844
- Maybe they know him more
as like Mee-chi-el Bub-lay?

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:01.677
(Kristina laughs)

00:03:01.677 --> 00:03:02.860
How do you say voice
of an angel in Russian?

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.885
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:03:04.885 --> 00:03:06.496
- (speaks foreign language)

00:03:06.496 --> 00:03:11.496
♪ And I promise you kids that I
give so much more than I get ♪

00:03:11.552 --> 00:03:14.358
♪ I just haven't met you yet ♪

00:03:14.358 --> 00:03:16.559
How do you feel the day has gone so far?

00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:18.809
- Very hot in Moscow today,

00:03:19.047 --> 00:03:22.597
but I like the time that
we're spending together.

00:03:22.597 --> 00:03:23.430
- When we've been filming,

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.068
you look at me like I'm a crazy person.

00:03:25.068 --> 00:03:26.279
- (laughs) You're funny.

00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:27.692
- There's a lot of
stereotypes about Russia.

00:03:27.692 --> 00:03:29.047
I mean, are there any stereotypes

00:03:29.047 --> 00:03:31.452
or myths you can debunk for us?

00:03:31.452 --> 00:03:36.210
- In our country and in our
cities, we don't live in bears.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.428
- (speaks in foreign language)

00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:39.928
- We don't have bears as pets.

00:03:40.077 --> 00:03:41.489
- (speaks foreign language)

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:42.949
- [Kristina] No bears in the streets!

00:03:42.949 --> 00:03:44.423
- Everyone keeps talking about the bears.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.124
- Look around, look around, where's?

00:03:46.124 --> 00:03:46.957
Bears!

00:03:46.957 --> 00:03:48.311
(roaring) Where are you?

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:49.519
Where the bears?

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:51.584
- (speaks foreign language)

00:03:51.584 --> 00:03:53.606
- There may be a stereotype
that we are gloomy

00:03:53.606 --> 00:03:56.189
and not friendly but we're nice

00:03:56.949 --> 00:03:58.352
and we like foreigners.

00:03:58.352 --> 00:04:01.352
- We are open to different cultures.

00:04:01.905 --> 00:04:03.464
- [Aria] But how do Russians actually feel

00:04:03.464 --> 00:04:05.239
about the United States?

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:08.529
A country with whom they have
such a complicated history.

00:04:08.529 --> 00:04:10.686
- I'm in love with the U.S.

00:04:10.686 --> 00:04:13.231
I've been an exchange
student for one year in Utah.

00:04:13.231 --> 00:04:14.123
- Oh, you lived in Utah?

00:04:14.123 --> 00:04:17.466
- Yes, exactly. For one
year. I was 16 back then

00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:19.743
and I used to live in the Mormon family,

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:22.241
and it was the best time of my life.

00:04:22.241 --> 00:04:24.127
- When I think about America,

00:04:24.127 --> 00:04:27.127
I remember about American Hollywood,

00:04:28.608 --> 00:04:31.275
American sport, but no negative.

00:04:32.127 --> 00:04:33.127
No negative.

00:04:33.132 --> 00:04:34.345
- It depends on the generation.

00:04:34.345 --> 00:04:36.215
Perhaps for the older generation,

00:04:36.215 --> 00:04:38.004
they kind of, strictly,

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:40.077
they don't like the politics.

00:04:40.077 --> 00:04:41.343
- I think it's politics.

00:04:41.343 --> 00:04:42.459
- Yes.
- To be honest.

00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:43.773
- It's all part of politics.

00:04:43.773 --> 00:04:46.940
- I know some people, maybe one or two

00:04:47.585 --> 00:04:49.364
who say something worse about U.S.

00:04:49.364 --> 00:04:51.942
but it's not my friends
this is another people,

00:04:51.942 --> 00:04:54.685
and this is people who never been in U.S.

00:04:54.685 --> 00:04:56.159
- And if an American is watching
this, what would you hope

00:04:56.159 --> 00:04:57.953
that they learn or take away about Russia?

00:04:57.953 --> 00:05:01.046
- That Russian people are very open-minded

00:05:01.046 --> 00:05:02.279
and they're kind.

00:05:02.279 --> 00:05:03.782
- That you are people and we are people.

00:05:03.782 --> 00:05:06.125
- (speaks in foreign language)

00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:08.708
- The best in world it's peace.

00:05:08.776 --> 00:05:11.859
And you want peace and we want peace.

00:05:12.072 --> 00:05:14.767
- Guys from U.S., guys from Russia,

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:18.889
we are friends forever and
ever and ever and ever.

00:05:18.889 --> 00:05:20.889
Russia and U.S. forever.

00:05:22.263 --> 00:05:23.237
- That was really moving, man.

00:05:23.237 --> 00:05:24.237
- Thank you.

00:05:24.912 --> 00:05:27.320
(happy music)

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.444
- [Aria] Russia is
country embroiled in a lot

00:05:29.444 --> 00:05:32.679
of controversy, and a day
in Moscow is hardly enough

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:36.429
to capture everything
about an entire nation.

00:05:36.633 --> 00:05:39.023
And while this video can
only provide a small slice

00:05:39.023 --> 00:05:41.883
of life here, I'm glad
today gave me a chance

00:05:41.883 --> 00:05:44.578
to meet some great people who, ultimately,

00:05:44.578 --> 00:05:47.401
proved to be no different than you or me

00:05:47.401 --> 00:05:49.931
or most others on this silly planet.

00:05:49.931 --> 00:05:52.259
So for now, I'll just leave you

00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:55.384
with some wise words from a Russian cat.

00:05:55.384 --> 00:05:56.217
(Russian folk music)

00:05:56.217 --> 00:06:00.384
- [Cat] (speaks foreign language)

00:06:00.641 --> 00:06:04.224
(happy Russian folk music)

00:06:09.279 --> 00:06:10.417
- [Aria] Do you hug in Russia?

00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:13.113
(woman laughs)
- Yes.

